  <h1>Model FLOP Utilization (MFU)</h1>
  <p class="lead"><strong>MFU</strong> answers the question: of all the floating-point operations your GPU is theoretically capable of, what fraction are actually doing useful model computation? It's the definitive measure of training efficiency — more informative than GPU utilization %, faster to compute than wall-clock benchmarks, and directly actionable. This post walks through the formula, the math behind it, and a real Llama 2 example from first principles.</p>
