<p>GPT-NeoX at 21% reflects an early A100 cluster without optimized interconnect. Llama 2 at 38.8% is solid but not exceptional — Meta traded some efficiency for simple infrastructure. PaLM's 46.2% is noteworthy given the 540B scale, achieved through TPU v4's high-bandwidth ICI interconnect and Google's optimized XLA compilation. FlashAttention-2 pushes into the 50s by dramatically reducing HBM traffic for attention, unlocking larger effective batch sizes and better compute-to-memory ratio.</p>

<h3>What to Target</h3>
<p>For most teams on A100/H100 hardware with model sizes from 7B–70B:</p>
<ul>
  <li>A fresh baseline without optimization: <strong>15–25% MFU</strong> is typical</li>
  <li>With FlashAttention, fused kernels, and proper batch sizing: <strong>35–45%</strong></li>
  <li>With NVLink-optimized tensor parallelism (Megatron-style): <strong>45–55%</strong></li>
  <li>H100 with FP8 training and well-tuned pipeline: pushing <strong>50–60%+</strong></li>
</ul>
</section>

<!-- Listen-friendly content (hidden summary played during audio playback) -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display: none;" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: Model FLOP Utilization Explained</h2>
    <p>Welcome to this audio summary explaining Model FLOP Utilization, or MFU, a key metric for measuring LLM training efficiency.</p>
    <p>When training large language models on costly GPU clusters, keeping the GPUs active and computing at peak capacity is critical. MFU represents the fraction of a GPU's theoretical peak floating-point operations per second that is actually spent performing useful model weight calculations.</p>
    <p>The standard way to calculate the numerator of MFU is the six N rule, which states that each training token requires six FLOPs per parameter: two FLOPs for the forward pass, and four FLOPs for the backward pass. Multiplying six by the parameter count and the training token count yields the total model FLOPs. This is then divided by the total theoretical peak FLOP capacity of all GPUs over the training duration.</p>
    <p>Hardware and memory bottlenecks usually prevent achieving one hundred percent utilization. Unoptimized clusters typically operate around fifteen to twenty-five percent MFU. By using optimizations like FlashAttention, kernel fusing, and careful batch sizing, teams can reach thirty-five to forty-five percent MFU. High-end setups using tensor parallelism or FP8 precision on H100 hardware can push MFU into the fifty to sixty percent range, cutting total training time and cost in half compared to basic setups.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：模型浮点利用率（MFU）深度解析</h2>
    <p>欢迎收听本期语音摘要，今天我们来深入解析“模型浮点利用率”（Model FLOP Utilization，简称 MFU）。这是衡量大语言模型训练效率的核心指标。</p>
    <p>在昂贵的 GPU 集群上训练大模型时，最大化 GPU 的实际计算效率至关重要。MFU 指标衡量了在 GPU 的理论峰值算力中，有多少比例真正用在了有用的模型参数计算上。</p>
    <p>计算 MFU 分子的标准方法是 6N 规则：每个训练 Token 对应每个参数需要消耗 6 个 FLOPs 的计算量（其中前向传播 2 个，反向传播 4 个）。将 6 乘以参数量和 Token 总数即可得到模型的有用浮点运算总量。再将其除以训练期间所有 GPU 的理论总算力，即得出 MFU 百分比。</p>
    <p>在实际训练中，硬件通信和内存带宽瓶颈会导致大量 GPU 空闲。未优化的集群 MFU 通常只有百分之十五到二十五。通过引入 FlashAttention、算子融合以及优化 Batch Size，可以提升到百分之三十五到四十五。而在 H100 硬件上使用张量并行和 FP8 精度进行联合调优，MFU 可以突破百分之五十至六十，相比未优化状态可将训练时间和资金成本减半。</p>
  </div>
</div>

